    "q-151162": {
      "dom_id": "step-q151162",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/495da285b0971f050ad2baa2031ef27a9d9fd719078f535559cb2795057516de.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides.",
      "worked_solution": "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that the lines $\\overset{⟷}{PQ}$ and  $\\overset{⟷}{TP}$ are perpendicular.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/db4497b62f456afacd78221d68a76200d18dedcfd1e3e7b73f64847e39a55ae9.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{TP}$ and $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are perpendicular. We can write this as follows: \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{TP}⊥\\overset{―}{PQ}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
