    "q-151165": {
      "dom_id": "step-q151165",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/d8af8bd4c928216d30d6ee1764139a86af1f7ac2ce6a01d9b98cb081a60ed322.png)\n\nIn the figure above, find the perpendicular sides.",
      "worked_solution": "Two lines are perpendicular if they intersect and form a ${90}^{∘}$ angle.\n\nFirst, notice that we have two sets of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{BC}$\n\n- $\\overset{⟷}{EA}$ is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/90902346a26d5120e13c3df8e841e4fb57c6006b6e6a4390e30c6ae41f18630c.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the sides $\\overset{―}{AB}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are perpendicular, and $\\overset{―}{EA}$ and $\\overset{―}{AB}$ are also perpendicular. We can write this as follows:\n\n$\\,$ $\\overset{―}{AB}⊥\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{EA}⊥\\overset{―}{AB}$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-151165-a",
